cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the EthicalAI catalogue or the EthicalHive auditing method, please cite it as below."
title: "EthicalAI: A Grounded Catalogue of AI Integrity Failure Modes"
authors:
  - family-names: Dan
    given-names: Alexandru
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
url: "https://ethicalai.alexandrudan.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/danlex/ethicalhive"
# License is a provisional recommendation pending author sign-off (see RELEASE.md).
# CC-BY-4.0 proposed for the catalogue data; Apache-2.0 proposed for the scripts.
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >
  A catalogue of 207 AI integrity failure modes, most framed as parallels to named human
  cognitive failures and organized by ten cognitive systems, linked by a relation graph of
  which mode violates which obligation, causes which harm, and relates to which neighbor,
  with a second tier of AI-native modes that have no human analogue. Every grounded mode is
  tied to a primary paper read rather than keyword-matched. Accompanied by two findings on
  the reliability of that grounding (citation drift and a verification sweep) and a
  clause-traceable advisory auditing method built on the catalogue.
keywords:
  - AI integrity
  - failure modes
  - taxonomy
  - LLM evaluation
  - cognitive bias
  - AI safety
